      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Objects and Edges\nAn object resource manages one Snowflake\nobject, such as `snowflake_database` or\n`snowflake_warehouse`. It has a computed\n`fully_qualified_name`. An edge resource\nmanages a relation between objects that it\ndoes not own, so it has no such field\n([identifier guide](https://github.com/snowfla\nkedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0\n/docs/guides/identifiers_rework_design_decisio\nns.md#L62-L65)). The provider has one edge\nresource for each kind of grant ([grant resour\nces](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-\nprovider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/gr\nants_redesign_design_decisions.md#L17-L30)):\n\n- `snowflake_grant_privileges_to_account_role`\ngrants privileges to an account role.\n-\n`snowflake_grant_privileges_to_database_role`\ngrants privileges to a database role.\n- `snowflake_grant_account_role` and\n`snowflake_grant_database_role` grant a role\nto a role or a user.\n- `snowflake_grant_ownership` moves ownership\nof objects to another role.\n- `snowflake_grant_privileges_to_share` and\n`snowflake_grant_application_role` cover\nshares and apps.\n\nAn edge depends on objects that may live\noutside Terraform. A grant can name a\nwarehouse that someone made by hand, or a\ntable that dbt made. The pitfall Grants on\nUnmanaged Objects shows what happens when such\nan object disappears.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-dfbc499eeb89",
      "originalText": "Objects and Edges\nAn object resource manages one Snowflake object, such as `snowflake_database` or `snowflake_warehouse`. It has a computed `fully_qualified_name`. An edge resource manages a relation between objects that it does not own, so it has no such field ([identifier guide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/identifiers_rework_design_decisions.md#L62-L65)). The provider has one edge resource for each kind of grant ([grant resources](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/grants_redesign_design_decisions.md#L17-L30)):\n\n- `snowflake_grant_privileges_to_account_role` grants privileges to an account role.\n- `snowflake_grant_privileges_to_database_role` grants privileges to a database role.\n- `snowflake_grant_account_role` and `snowflake_grant_database_role` grant a role to a role or a user.\n- `snowflake_grant_ownership` moves ownership of objects to another role.\n- `snowflake_grant_privileges_to_share` and `snowflake_grant_application_role` cover shares and apps.\n\nAn edge depends on objects that may live outside Terraform. A grant can name a warehouse that someone made by hand, or a table that dbt made. The pitfall Grants on Unmanaged Objects shows what happens when such an object disappears.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "objects-and-edges"
      }
    },
