      "text": "Names Are Exact Strings\nEvery field that holds an identifier is\ncase-sensitive ([identifier guide](https://git\nhub.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowfla\nke/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/identifiers_rework\n_design_decisions.md#L100-L106)). In Snowflake\nSQL, an unquoted name turns into upper case.\nSo `name = \"TEST\"` and `name = \"test\"` are two\ndifferent objects, and the second one needs\nquotes in every query. Quotes alone, however,\ncause no diff. The provider ignores the\ndifference between `AGENT_WH` and `\"AGENT_WH\"`\n([quoting](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terr\naform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/gui\ndes/identifiers_rework_design_decisions.md#L56\n-L60)).\n\nThe resource ID follows one rule. If one\nSnowflake identifier describes the object, the\nID is its fully qualified name. Otherwise the\nID joins all needed parts with pipes ([ID form\nat](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-p\nrovider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/ide\nntifiers_rework_design_decisions.md#L84-L88)).\nImport blocks use the same strings:\n\n| Resource | Import ID |\n| --- | --- |\n| Account object, such as a warehouse |\n`'\"NAME\"'` |\n| Schema | `'\"DB\".\"SCHEMA\"'` |\n| Schema object, such as a typed stage |\n`'\"DB\".\"SCHEMA\".\"OBJ\"'` |\n| Grant to an account role | seven parts with\npipes, as in the example below |\n| `snowflake_execute` | a random UUID\n([execute import](https://github.com/snowflake\ndb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/d\nocs/resources/execute.md#L154-L160)) |\n\nAbout the Sources shows how this grant was\nimported from a real account and planned:\n\n```text\n\"AGENT_READ_ONLY\"|false|false|USAGE|OnAccountO\nbject|WAREHOUSE|\"AGENT_WH\"\n```\n\nThe seven parts are the role,\n`with_grant_option`, `always_apply`, the\nprivileges, the kind of target, the object\ntype and the object name. The configuration\nsaid `account_role_name = \"AGENT_READ_ONLY\"`\nwithout quotes. The state stored\n`\"\\\"AGENT_READ_ONLY\\\"\"` with quotes, and the\nplan still reported \"No changes\".\n\nTo refer to another object, read its\n`fully_qualified_name` instead of joining\nnames by hand ([identifier guide](https://gith\nub.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflak\ne/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/identifiers_rework_\ndesign_decisions.md#L62-L83)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-707fb1d30b0b",
      "originalText": "Names Are Exact Strings\nEvery field that holds an identifier is case-sensitive ([identifier guide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/identifiers_rework_design_decisions.md#L100-L106)). In Snowflake SQL, an unquoted name turns into upper case. So `name = \"TEST\"` and `name = \"test\"` are two different objects, and the second one needs quotes in every query. Quotes alone, however, cause no diff. The provider ignores the difference between `AGENT_WH` and `\"AGENT_WH\"` ([quoting](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/identifiers_rework_design_decisions.md#L56-L60)).\n\nThe resource ID follows one rule. If one Snowflake identifier describes the object, the ID is its fully qualified name. Otherwise the ID joins all needed parts with pipes ([ID format](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/identifiers_rework_design_decisions.md#L84-L88)). Import blocks use the same strings:\n\n| Resource | Import ID |\n| --- | --- |\n| Account object, such as a warehouse | `'\"NAME\"'` |\n| Schema | `'\"DB\".\"SCHEMA\"'` |\n| Schema object, such as a typed stage | `'\"DB\".\"SCHEMA\".\"OBJ\"'` |\n| Grant to an account role | seven parts with pipes, as in the example below |\n| `snowflake_execute` | a random UUID ([execute import](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/resources/execute.md#L154-L160)) |\n\nAbout the Sources shows how this grant was imported from a real account and planned:\n\n```text\n\"AGENT_READ_ONLY\"|false|false|USAGE|OnAccountObject|WAREHOUSE|\"AGENT_WH\"\n```\n\nThe seven parts are the role, `with_grant_option`, `always_apply`, the privileges, the kind of target, the object type and the object name. The configuration said `account_role_name = \"AGENT_READ_ONLY\"` without quotes. The state stored `\"\\\"AGENT_READ_ONLY\\\"\"` with quotes, and the plan still reported \"No changes\".\n\nTo refer to another object, read its `fully_qualified_name` instead of joining names by hand ([identifier guide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/identifiers_rework_design_decisions.md#L62-L83)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "names-are-exact-strings"
      }
    },
