    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3821210246,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-42bfe12e8fad",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1288.8,
      "y": 900.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 700.0,
      "seed": 916855,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "State Holds Only What You Set\nThe provider does not store an optional\nargument that the configuration leaves out\n([config values in state](https://github.com/s\nnowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v\n2.23.0/v1-preparations/CHANGES_BEFORE_V1.md#L4\n6-L51)). Snowflake then keeps its own default\nfor it. To show those values, each resource\nhas three read-only outputs ([raw output](http\ns://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-\nsnowflake/blob/v2.23.0/v1-preparations/CHANGES\n_BEFORE_V1.md#L53-L59)):\n\n- `show_output` holds the result of `SHOW\n<objects>`.\n- `describe_output` holds the result of\n`DESCRIBE <object>`.\n- `parameters` holds the result of `SHOW\nPARAMETERS IN <object>`.\n\nSome arguments use special values for \"not\nset\" ([empty values](https://github.com/snowfl\nakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.\n0/v1-preparations/CHANGES_BEFORE_V1.md#L29-L34\n)):\n\n- `\"default\"` for a boolean that the provider\nstores as a string.\n- `-1` for a number whose valid range includes\n0, such as `auto_suspend`.\n- `\"<Snowflake Terraform Provider string\ndefault>\"` for a string that can be empty.\n\nThese values appear in plans. A plan that sets\nan argument to `\"default\"` asks Snowflake to\ngo back to its own default. The [Terraform map\n](../terraform.md#outside-changes-get-reverted\n-outside-changes-get-reverted) shows a real\nwarehouse plan with such lines. To keep a\nvalue, write it in the configuration.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-42bfe12e8fad",
      "originalText": "State Holds Only What You Set\nThe provider does not store an optional argument that the configuration leaves out ([config values in state](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/v1-preparations/CHANGES_BEFORE_V1.md#L46-L51)). Snowflake then keeps its own default for it. To show those values, each resource has three read-only outputs ([raw output](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/v1-preparations/CHANGES_BEFORE_V1.md#L53-L59)):\n\n- `show_output` holds the result of `SHOW <objects>`.\n- `describe_output` holds the result of `DESCRIBE <object>`.\n- `parameters` holds the result of `SHOW PARAMETERS IN <object>`.\n\nSome arguments use special values for \"not set\" ([empty values](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/v1-preparations/CHANGES_BEFORE_V1.md#L29-L34)):\n\n- `\"default\"` for a boolean that the provider stores as a string.\n- `-1` for a number whose valid range includes 0, such as `auto_suspend`.\n- `\"<Snowflake Terraform Provider string default>\"` for a string that can be empty.\n\nThese values appear in plans. A plan that sets an argument to `\"default\"` asks Snowflake to go back to its own default. The [Terraform map](../terraform.md#outside-changes-get-reverted-outside-changes-get-reverted) shows a real warehouse plan with such lines. To keep a value, write it in the configuration.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "state-holds-only-what-you-set"
      }
    },
