      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Versions and Stability\nThe provider's resources come in three tiers:\n\n- Stable resources are supported.\n- Preview resources work only when you list\nthem in `preview_features_enabled`. They can\nbreak in a minor version, and Snowflake does\nnot support them ([disclaimer](https://github.\ncom/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/b\nlob/v2.23.0/docs/index.md#L17)).\n- Experiments change provider behavior. Each\none starts as opt-in, then becomes the\ndefault, and then is promoted ([experiments](h\nttps://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provid\ner-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/index.md#L998-L\n1016)).\n\nSnowflake supports only the latest stable\nversion of the provider, from 2.0.0 onward\n([Snowflake Terraform provider](https://docs.s\nnowflake.com/en/user-guide/terraform)). Fixes\nfor Snowflake behavior changes therefore\narrive only in new versions. The version pin\nin `required_providers` is the support\nboundary.\n\nThe source address changed twice. It was\n`chanzuckerberg/snowflake`, then\n`Snowflake-Labs/snowflake` from 2022-05-25\n([CZI upgrade](https://github.com/snowflakedb/\nterraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/CZI_\nUPGRADE.md#L3-L7)), and now\n`snowflakedb/snowflake`. A team moves its\nstate to the new address with `terraform state\nreplace-provider Snowflake-Labs/snowflake\nsnowflakedb/snowflake` ([namespace migration](\nhttps://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provi\nder-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/SNOWFLAKEDB_MIGRATI\nON.md#L3-L9)). The old address stops at\nversion 1.0.5.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-e96c1efcc080",
      "originalText": "Versions and Stability\nThe provider's resources come in three tiers:\n\n- Stable resources are supported.\n- Preview resources work only when you list them in `preview_features_enabled`. They can break in a minor version, and Snowflake does not support them ([disclaimer](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/index.md#L17)).\n- Experiments change provider behavior. Each one starts as opt-in, then becomes the default, and then is promoted ([experiments](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/index.md#L998-L1016)).\n\nSnowflake supports only the latest stable version of the provider, from 2.0.0 onward ([Snowflake Terraform provider](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/terraform)). Fixes for Snowflake behavior changes therefore arrive only in new versions. The version pin in `required_providers` is the support boundary.\n\nThe source address changed twice. It was `chanzuckerberg/snowflake`, then `Snowflake-Labs/snowflake` from 2022-05-25 ([CZI upgrade](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/CZI_UPGRADE.md#L3-L7)), and now `snowflakedb/snowflake`. A team moves its state to the new address with `terraform state replace-provider Snowflake-Labs/snowflake snowflakedb/snowflake` ([namespace migration](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/SNOWFLAKEDB_MIGRATION.md#L3-L9)). The old address stops at version 1.0.5.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "versions-and-stability"
      }
    },
