      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Two-Step Trust with AWS\nThree Snowflake objects act in AWS through an\nIAM role: a storage integration for stages and\nSnowpipe, an external volume for Iceberg\ntables, and a notification integration. The\n[Iceberg in Snowflake map](../../snowflake/ice\nberg/snowflake-iceberg.md) explains external\nvolumes and catalog integrations.\n\nEach side needs a value from the other side.\nSnowflake must know the role ARN. The role's\ntrust policy must name Snowflake's IAM user\nand an external ID. Snowflake uses one IAM\nuser for each account ([storage integration gu\nide](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/\ndata-load-s3-config-storage-integration)).\nConfigurations break this loop in one of three\nways:\n\n1. They apply twice. Someone copies\nSnowflake's IAM user ARN and external ID into\nthe AWS code between the two applies.\n2. They fix the role ARN in advance by a\nnaming rule. The integration is created first,\nand the trust policy then reads\n`describe_output` of the integration.\n3. They choose the external ID themselves with\n`STORAGE_AWS_EXTERNAL_ID`. Both sides then\nknow every value before the first apply.\nSnowflake documents this option so that one\nexternal ID can serve several integrations and\nvolumes.\n\nThe [AWS map](../aws/terraform-aws.md)\nexplains the IAM side of the trust.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-1dce855e68a4",
      "originalText": "Two-Step Trust with AWS\nThree Snowflake objects act in AWS through an IAM role: a storage integration for stages and Snowpipe, an external volume for Iceberg tables, and a notification integration. The [Iceberg in Snowflake map](../../snowflake/iceberg/snowflake-iceberg.md) explains external volumes and catalog integrations.\n\nEach side needs a value from the other side. Snowflake must know the role ARN. The role's trust policy must name Snowflake's IAM user and an external ID. Snowflake uses one IAM user for each account ([storage integration guide](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/data-load-s3-config-storage-integration)). Configurations break this loop in one of three ways:\n\n1. They apply twice. Someone copies Snowflake's IAM user ARN and external ID into the AWS code between the two applies.\n2. They fix the role ARN in advance by a naming rule. The integration is created first, and the trust policy then reads `describe_output` of the integration.\n3. They choose the external ID themselves with `STORAGE_AWS_EXTERNAL_ID`. Both sides then know every value before the first apply. Snowflake documents this option so that one external ID can serve several integrations and volumes.\n\nThe [AWS map](../aws/terraform-aws.md) explains the IAM side of the trust.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "two-step-trust-with-aws"
      }
    },
