      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2298589487,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-7053beadabe1",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 2460.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 577.5,
      "seed": 786834,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Plan Signals\n| Line in the plan | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `-/+` on `snowflake_execute` | Any change to\n`execute` replaces the resource: Terraform\nruns `revert`, then `execute` ([execute.go](ht\ntps://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provide\nr-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/pkg/resources/execute\n.go#L63-L65)). |\n| `\"default\"` or `-1` as a new value | The\nargument goes back to the Snowflake default. |\n| `(known after apply)` on `describe_output` |\nAn argument that feeds the output changed\n([storage integration](https://github.com/snow\nflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.2\n3.0/pkg/resources/storage_integration_aws.go#L\n131-L132)). On schemas it can appear in every\nplan when the role cannot see the objects\ninside ([issue 3296](https://github.com/snowfl\nakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/issues/3296\n)). |\n| A grant that appears in every plan | The\ngrant sets `always_apply`, which grants again\nat each apply ([warning](https://github.com/sn\nowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2\n.23.0/docs/resources/grant_privileges_to_accou\nnt_role.md#L9)). |\n| `(sensitive value)` in place of SQL | A\nsensitive variable inside the SQL hides the\nwhole string from review. |\n| `# forces replacement` on a database, schema\nor integration | Terraform drops the object\nand creates it again. |",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-7053beadabe1",
      "originalText": "Plan Signals\n| Line in the plan | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `-/+` on `snowflake_execute` | Any change to `execute` replaces the resource: Terraform runs `revert`, then `execute` ([execute.go](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/pkg/resources/execute.go#L63-L65)). |\n| `\"default\"` or `-1` as a new value | The argument goes back to the Snowflake default. |\n| `(known after apply)` on `describe_output` | An argument that feeds the output changed ([storage integration](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/pkg/resources/storage_integration_aws.go#L131-L132)). On schemas it can appear in every plan when the role cannot see the objects inside ([issue 3296](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/issues/3296)). |\n| A grant that appears in every plan | The grant sets `always_apply`, which grants again at each apply ([warning](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/resources/grant_privileges_to_account_role.md#L9)). |\n| `(sensitive value)` in place of SQL | A sensitive variable inside the SQL hides the whole string from review. |\n| `# forces replacement` on a database, schema or integration | Terraform drops the object and creates it again. |",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "snowflake-plan-signals"
      }
    },
