    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6986106945,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-c2179dc406e4",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1940.8,
      "y": 2720.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 297.5,
      "seed": 180117,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "No Drift Detection\nA refresh of `snowflake_execute` runs only\n`query` and stores the rows in `query_results`\n([read code](https://github.com/snowflakedb/te\nrraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/pkg/re\nsources/execute.go#L109-L161)). So if someone\ndrops the object or revokes the grant by hand,\nthe plan stays empty. A failing `query` gives\nonly a warning ([note](https://github.com/snow\nflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.2\n3.0/docs/resources/execute.md#L18)). `query`\nalso does not decide whether `execute` runs.\nWith `CREATE ... IF NOT EXISTS`, a changed\ndefinition does nothing when the object\nexists. Check the real object with `SHOW` or\n`DESCRIBE`, and prefer a native resource when\none exists.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-c2179dc406e4",
      "originalText": "No Drift Detection\nA refresh of `snowflake_execute` runs only `query` and stores the rows in `query_results` ([read code](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/pkg/resources/execute.go#L109-L161)). So if someone drops the object or revokes the grant by hand, the plan stays empty. A failing `query` gives only a warning ([note](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/resources/execute.md#L18)). `query` also does not decide whether `execute` runs. With `CREATE ... IF NOT EXISTS`, a changed definition does nothing when the object exists. Check the real object with `SHOW` or `DESCRIBE`, and prefer a native resource when one exists.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "execute-no-drift-detection"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8314332254,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-00de5811b99e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1928.8,
      "y": 2980.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "#FEF3C7",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220.0,
      "seed": 836691,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
