    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4959798580,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-00de5811b99e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1940.8,
      "y": 2980.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 332.5,
      "seed": 244815,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "An Edit Drops and Recreates\nAny change to the `execute` text replaces the\nresource. Terraform runs `revert` and then the\nnew `execute` ([execute.go](https://github.com\n/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob\n/v2.23.0/pkg/resources/execute.go#L63-L65); [d\nelete](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terrafor\nm-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/pkg/resource\ns/execute.go#L163-L176)). A rotated OAuth\nsecret inside a `CREATE CATALOG INTEGRATION`\nstatement is such a change. Snowflake refuses\nto drop or replace a catalog integration while\nIceberg tables use it ([DROP CATALOG INTEGRATI\nON](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-referenc\ne/sql/drop-catalog-integration)), so the apply\nfails halfway. `ALTER CATALOG INTEGRATION ...\nSET` changes the secret in place, and so does\nthe native resource\n`snowflake_catalog_integration_open_catalog`.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-00de5811b99e",
      "originalText": "An Edit Drops and Recreates\nAny change to the `execute` text replaces the resource. Terraform runs `revert` and then the new `execute` ([execute.go](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/pkg/resources/execute.go#L63-L65); [delete](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/pkg/resources/execute.go#L163-L176)). A rotated OAuth secret inside a `CREATE CATALOG INTEGRATION` statement is such a change. Snowflake refuses to drop or replace a catalog integration while Iceberg tables use it ([DROP CATALOG INTEGRATION](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/sql/drop-catalog-integration)), so the apply fails halfway. `ALTER CATALOG INTEGRATION ... SET` changes the secret in place, and so does the native resource `snowflake_catalog_integration_open_catalog`.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "execute-edit-recreates"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5583820121,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-4404ce68408e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
