    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9379645159,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-19037c3413e0",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1332.0,
      "y": 3951.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 386.40000000000003,
      "height": 87.5,
      "seed": 122028,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Grant Pitfalls\nThese pitfalls change who can read what. Three\nof the four pass the apply without an error,\nand users notice them later as missing\nprivileges.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-19037c3413e0",
      "originalText": "Grant Pitfalls\nThese pitfalls change who can read what. Three of the four pass the apply without an error, and users notice them later as missing privileges.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "grant-pitfalls"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4229254360,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-ed4a2fbb4f9d",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1920.4,
      "y": 3496.5,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "#FEF3C7",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220.0,
      "seed": 589502,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
        "value": 8
      },
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text-ed4a2fbb4f9d"
        },
        {
          "id": "edge-1b30806fd6a8",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "edge-535eb3e6680a",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "schema-level-future-grants-win"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5801817892,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-ed4a2fbb4f9d",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1932.4,
      "y": 3496.5,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 315.0,
      "seed": 292557,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Schema-Level Future Grants Win\nWhen a database and one of its schemas both\nhave future grants for the same object type,\nSnowflake uses only the schema-level grants.\nIt ignores the database-level ones in that\nschema, for every role ([future grants](https:\n//docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/sql/gran\nt-privilege)). So one schema-level future\ngrant, made by anyone, silently turns off the\ndatabase-level future grants of every other\nrole there. New tables in that schema then\nlack the expected privileges. Check with `SHOW\nFUTURE GRANTS IN SCHEMA <db>.<schema>`. The\nsame rule applies to future ownership since\nbehavior change bundle BCR-1870\n([grant_ownership note](https://github.com/sno\nwflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.\n23.0/docs/resources/grant_ownership.md#L12)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-ed4a2fbb4f9d",
      "originalText": "Schema-Level Future Grants Win\nWhen a database and one of its schemas both have future grants for the same object type, Snowflake uses only the schema-level grants. It ignores the database-level ones in that schema, for every role ([future grants](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/sql/grant-privilege)). So one schema-level future grant, made by anyone, silently turns off the database-level future grants of every other role there. New tables in that schema then lack the expected privileges. Check with `SHOW FUTURE GRANTS IN SCHEMA <db>.<schema>`. The same rule applies to future ownership since behavior change bundle BCR-1870 ([grant_ownership note](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/resources/grant_ownership.md#L12)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "schema-level-future-grants-win"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4598744351,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-b2ea5d61c4d7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1920.4,
      "y": 3756.5,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "#FEF3C7",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220.0,
      "seed": 469510,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
        "value": 8
      },
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text-b2ea5d61c4d7"
        },
        {
          "id": "edge-8876e7e24f4f",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
