      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Cascading Drops\n`DROP SCHEMA` uses `CASCADE` by default, so it\ndrops every object in the schema ([DROP SCHEMA\n](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/\nsql/drop-schema)). A schema that dbt fills is\ntherefore one destroy away from losing all its\ntables. Moving a schema to another database\nrecreates it ([renaming guide](https://github.\ncom/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/b\nlob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/object_renaming_guide.\nmd#L21-L47)). Recovery is a manual `UNDROP`\nwithin the Time Travel period, then an import\n([restore guide](https://github.com/snowflaked\nb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/do\ncs/guides/restoring_lost_data.md#L42-L50)).\nTime Travel keeps data for 1 day by default\n([Time Travel](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/u\nser-guide/data-time-travel)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-4e48778f677b",
      "originalText": "Cascading Drops\n`DROP SCHEMA` uses `CASCADE` by default, so it drops every object in the schema ([DROP SCHEMA](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/sql/drop-schema)). A schema that dbt fills is therefore one destroy away from losing all its tables. Moving a schema to another database recreates it ([renaming guide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/object_renaming_guide.md#L21-L47)). Recovery is a manual `UNDROP` within the Time Travel period, then an import ([restore guide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/restoring_lost_data.md#L42-L50)). Time Travel keeps data for 1 day by default ([Time Travel](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/data-time-travel)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "cascading-drops"
      }
    },
