      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Case-Sensitive Names\nA lower-case name in Terraform creates a\nlower-case object. For example, `name =\n\"tags\"` creates the schema `\"tags\"`. Then\n`SHOW SCHEMAS LIKE 'TAGS'` and every unquoted\n`tags` in SQL miss it. The identifier guide\nshows the same trap with a role ([identifier g\nuide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform\n-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/i\ndentifiers_rework_design_decisions.md#L100-L10\n6)). Write names in upper case unless a\nlower-case name is intended.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-20dc165e649b",
      "originalText": "Case-Sensitive Names\nA lower-case name in Terraform creates a lower-case object. For example, `name = \"tags\"` creates the schema `\"tags\"`. Then `SHOW SCHEMAS LIKE 'TAGS'` and every unquoted `tags` in SQL miss it. The identifier guide shows the same trap with a role ([identifier guide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/guides/identifiers_rework_design_decisions.md#L100-L106)). Write names in upper case unless a lower-case name is intended.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "case-sensitive-names"
      }
    },
    {
