    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2844344760,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-08df68b453ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1873.6,
      "y": 5833.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 682.5,
      "seed": 571469,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Old Pins and Preview Resources\nAn old provider pin keeps old bugs and old\ndefaults:\n\n- Before 2.23.0, a new warehouse without\n`warehouse_type` gets Snowflake's default\ntype. Snowflake is changing that default from\nSTANDARD to ADAPTIVE. Since 2.23.0 the\nprovider sends STANDARD ([migration guide](htt\nps://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider\n-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/MIGRATION_GUIDE.md#L30\n7-L330)).\n- Before 2.22.0, safe destroy of grants is\nopt-in (see Grants on Unmanaged Objects).\n- A preview resource can break in a minor\nversion. `snowflake_table` is one ([disclaimer\n](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-pro\nvider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/index.md#L17\n)).\n- On the deprecated `snowflake_stage`, a\nchange of `directory` recreates the stage,\nwhich can break its pipes ([issue 4059](https:\n//github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-sn\nowflake/issues/4059)).\n- Snowflake behavior change bundles (BCRs) can\ncreate drift. With BCR-2371 enabled, `SHOW\nGRANTS` reports an Iceberg table as `ICEBERG\nTABLE`. A database-role grant that names it\nwith `object_type = \"TABLE\"` then shows a\npermanent diff ([BCR guide](https://github.com\n/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob\n/v2.23.0/SNOWFLAKE_BCR_MIGRATION_GUIDE.md#L69-\nL100)).\n\nEach minor version has a section in the\n[migration guide](https://github.com/snowflake\ndb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/M\nIGRATION_GUIDE.md). Read it before you raise\nthe pin.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-08df68b453ff",
      "originalText": "Old Pins and Preview Resources\nAn old provider pin keeps old bugs and old defaults:\n\n- Before 2.23.0, a new warehouse without `warehouse_type` gets Snowflake's default type. Snowflake is changing that default from STANDARD to ADAPTIVE. Since 2.23.0 the provider sends STANDARD ([migration guide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/MIGRATION_GUIDE.md#L307-L330)).\n- Before 2.22.0, safe destroy of grants is opt-in (see Grants on Unmanaged Objects).\n- A preview resource can break in a minor version. `snowflake_table` is one ([disclaimer](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/docs/index.md#L17)).\n- On the deprecated `snowflake_stage`, a change of `directory` recreates the stage, which can break its pipes ([issue 4059](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/issues/4059)).\n- Snowflake behavior change bundles (BCRs) can create drift. With BCR-2371 enabled, `SHOW GRANTS` reports an Iceberg table as `ICEBERG TABLE`. A database-role grant that names it with `object_type = \"TABLE\"` then shows a permanent diff ([BCR guide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/SNOWFLAKE_BCR_MIGRATION_GUIDE.md#L69-L100)).\n\nEach minor version has a section in the [migration guide](https://github.com/snowflakedb/terraform-provider-snowflake/blob/v2.23.0/MIGRATION_GUIDE.md). Read it before you raise the pin.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "old-pins-and-preview-resources"
      }
    },
