    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 7769455854,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-e2ef693d4c46",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 730.0,
      "y": 7389.5,
      "strokeColor": "#57534E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 397.8,
      "height": 666.25,
      "seed": 993554,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "About the Sources\nThe provider facts come from the\n`snowflakedb/snowflake` repository at tag v2.23.0,\nthe latest release on 2026-11-23. The Snowflake\nfacts come from docs.snowflake.com on the same day.\n\nThe grant example ran on 2026-11-23 with Terraform\n1.15.8 and provider 2.23.0, against a real account\nand with a read-only role. Terraform only read the\ngrant and wrote a local state file. The folder held\nthe `terraform.tf`, `providers.tf` and\n`variables.tf` files from the About the Examples\nnode of the [Terraform map](../terraform.md), and\nthis `main.tf`:\n\n```hcl\nresource\n\"snowflake_grant_privileges_to_account_role\"\n\"agent_wh_usage\" {\naccount_role_name = \"AGENT_READ_ONLY\"\nprivileges        = [\"USAGE\"]\n\non_account_object {\nobject_type = \"WAREHOUSE\"\nobject_name = \"AGENT_WH\"\n}\n}\n```\n\nThese commands ran with the same `TF_VAR_`\nenvironment variables as in that node:\n\n```bash\nterraform init -input=false\nterraform import snowflake_grant_privileges_to_acco\nunt_role.agent_wh_usage '\"AGENT_READ_ONLY\"|false|fa\nlse|USAGE|OnAccountObject|WAREHOUSE|\"AGENT_WH\"'\nterraform plan -input=false\nterraform state show snowflake_grant_privileges_to_\naccount_role.agent_wh_usage\n```",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 16.25,
      "containerId": "node-e2ef693d4c46",
      "originalText": "About the Sources\nThe provider facts come from the `snowflakedb/snowflake` repository at tag v2.23.0, the latest release on 2026-11-23. The Snowflake facts come from docs.snowflake.com on the same day.\n\nThe grant example ran on 2026-11-23 with Terraform 1.15.8 and provider 2.23.0, against a real account and with a read-only role. Terraform only read the grant and wrote a local state file. The folder held the `terraform.tf`, `providers.tf` and `variables.tf` files from the About the Examples node of the [Terraform map](../terraform.md), and this `main.tf`:\n\n```hcl\nresource \"snowflake_grant_privileges_to_account_role\" \"agent_wh_usage\" {\n  account_role_name = \"AGENT_READ_ONLY\"\n  privileges        = [\"USAGE\"]\n\n  on_account_object {\n    object_type = \"WAREHOUSE\"\n    object_name = \"AGENT_WH\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThese commands ran with the same `TF_VAR_` environment variables as in that node:\n\n```bash\nterraform init -input=false\nterraform import snowflake_grant_privileges_to_account_role.agent_wh_usage '\"AGENT_READ_ONLY\"|false|false|USAGE|OnAccountObject|WAREHOUSE|\"AGENT_WH\"'\nterraform plan -input=false\nterraform state show snowflake_grant_privileges_to_account_role.agent_wh_usage\n```",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "snowflake-about-the-sources"
      }
    },
